  "narrative": "All returned estimates are already signed to the registered hypothesis direction. For direction -1 claims, a positive signed estimate means the exposed state is associated with a more negative, stronger CRISPR dependency score; for the direction +1 NFE2L2 claim, a positive signed estimate is consistent with the accepted weaker NFE2L2 dependency direction after KEAP1 loss. No new independent validation can be requested because the voluntary validation budget is exhausted, so these are discovery-evidence assessments and do not establish causality or external generalizability. I use a practical benchmark of roughly 0.10 dependency-score units, which is conservative relative to a 10% relative change for these centered negative scores, and I require the interval and point estimate to support a meaningful difference rather than merely a small statistical deviation. H267 is near null, +0.0066 [-0.0192, 0.0324], with the confidence interval including no effect and the upper bound well below the practical benchmark. If the delivered stratum is the intended low-context CDKN2A-MDM2 cell, this supports the emerging pattern that high research_signature_c is the main context driver rather than a broad high-signature context. However, the displayed H267 eligibility appears to overlap an earlier accepted low-9p21 stratum while the delivered cell counts differ, so I flag this as a registration or display ambiguity. I do not use this null result to overturn the validated CDKN2A-MDM2 main association, but I registered an explicit low-signature-c and low-signature-a stratum to remove the ambiguity. H268 gives a large CDKN2A-loss MDM2 effect in high signature_c and high signature_a, +0.490 [0.340, 0.641], supporting that high signature_c concentrates the association even when signature_a is also high. Together with the rejected high-signature-a/low-signature-c stratum, this favors signature-c-specific context modification rather than a generic signature_a amplifier for MDM2. H269 is a higher-n sensitivity analysis for PTEN-loss STAT3 in high signature_a using a lower signature_c threshold, +0.549 [0.386, 0.713] with only 29 exposed cells. The interval is entirely above the practical benchmark, so I accept it with caution about small-cell precision. This continues to support high signature_a as an amplifier of PTEN-loss STAT3 dependency. H270 through H273 are direct high-signature-a strata for the core USP7, SMARCA2, WRN, and NFE2L2 axes. All four are very large and intervals are far above the practical benchmark: USP7 +0.823 [0.788, 0.857], SMARCA2 +0.785 [0.750, 0.819], WRN +0.799 [0.739, 0.860], and NFE2L2 direction +1 +0.798 [0.758, 0.837]. These support that the core dependencies remain extremely strong in high signature_a, and they do not indicate that signature_a generally attenuates the core axes. The high-signature-a amplification is most distinctive for PTEN-loss STAT3. H272 has only 31 exposed MSI-high cells, but the interval is so far above the benchmark that acceptance is reasonable within this dataset. H274 tests whether the high-signature-c CDKN2A-MDM2 association is modified by batch_a, +0.003 [-0.076, 0.081]. This is small, statistically unresolved, and the upper bound is below the practical benchmark, so I reject it as a meaningful interaction. H275 and H276 show that the high-signature-c CDKN2A-MDM2 effect remains large in lower screen-quality cells and in KY-library cells, +0.336 [0.207, 0.466] and +0.305 [0.134, 0.475] respectively; I accept both, with caution in H276 because exposed n is 27. These support technical robustness of the signature_c context effect, although they remain within-dataset associations. H27, TP53 loss for KIF18A dependency, is signed positive, +0.021 [0.001, 0.040]. It may be statistically small-positive, but the point estimate is far below the practical benchmark and the interval does not robustly exceed even a relative 10% scale for this outcome. I reject it as scientifically or practically meaningful. H28, MYC amplification for RPL11 dependency, is opposite the registered direction and unresolved, -0.012 [-0.034, 0.009], so I reject it. Overall, the new evidence strengthens the core dependency associations, refines the constructed-signature context interpretation, and rejects small residual direct effects that are statistically detectable but not practically meaningful.",
  "research_notes": "Iteration 20 appraisal complete. Validation budget exhausted. H267 null is rejected but flagged for eligibility-display ambiguity; explicit low signature_c and low signature_a CDKN2A-MDM2 comparison registered to confirm signature-c specificity. High signature_a CDKN2A-MDM2 accepted; core USP7, SMARCA2, WRN, and NFE2L2 axes remain enormous in high signature_a, supporting axis-specific signature_a amplification for PTEN-STAT3 rather than generic attenuation of core axes. High signature_c MDM2 context is robust in lower-quality screens and KY library; batch_a interaction null. KIF18A-TP53 and RPL11-MYC are practically non-meaningful. Next useful analyses are low signature_a strata for core axes and the explicit low signature_c and low signature_a CDKN2A-MDM2 context cell. All conclusions remain within-dataset associations and do not establish causality or external generalizability."
